====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Something that is number two in a [[series]].
# Something that is next in rank, [[quality]], [[precedence]], position, status, or authority.
# The place that is next below or after first in a race or contest.
# {{lb|en|usually|in the plural}} A [[manufactured]] item that, though still usable, fails to meet [[quality control]] standards.
#: {{ux|en|They were discounted because they contained blemishes, nicks or were otherwise factory '''seconds'''.}}
# {{lb|en|usually|in the plural}} An additional helping of food.
#: {{ux|en|That was good barbecue. I hope I can get '''seconds'''.}}
# A chance or attempt to achieve what should have been done the first time, usually indicating success this time around. (See [[second-guess]].)
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Sheila Ryan Wallace|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=_-FT12DfGfoC&pg=PA22&dq=%22That's+what+got+you+in+trouble+the+first+time+around.+You+don't+need+a+second.%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=1ZM8UpeaEe644AP1r4FA&ved=0CC8Q6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=%22That's%20what%20got%20you%20in%20trouble%20the%20first%20time%20around.%20You%20don't%20need%20a%20second.%22&f=false|title=The Sea Captain and His Ladies|page=22|passage=The policeman smiled, his eyes twinkling. "Now if you'll follow me, I'll escort you to the Victoria."<br/>"Oh, there's no need of that. If you'll just point me in the right direction..."<br/>That's what got you in trouble the first time around. You don't need a '''second'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Paulette Jiles|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=Yv4lqGxp1iwC&pg=PT48&dq=%22Maybe+once.+But+you+don't+get+a+second.%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=B548UurMGM-y4APdmICgCA&ved=0CC8Q6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=%22Maybe%20once.%20But%20you%20don't%20get%20a%20second.%22&f=false|title=Stormy Weather|page=37|passage=Smoky Joe ran against a Houston horse named Cherokee Chief.<br/>“Don't hit him,” Jeanine said to the jockey. “Maybe once. But you don't get a '''second'''.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Karen Miller|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=fRavxPlf7KIC&pg=PT402&dq=%22one+chance%22+%22get+a+second%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=YuE9UsDxKqWR2wX2k4GoDw&ved=0CDYQ6AEwAjgU#v=onepage&q=%22one%20chance%22%20%22get%20a%20second%22&f=false|title=The Innocent Mage|passage=I'll have one chance to show them that's no longer true. One chance ... and if I stumble, I'll not get a '''second'''.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} The interval between two adjacent notes in a [[diatonic]] scale (either or both of them may be raised or lowered from the basic scale via any type of [[accidental]]).
# The [[second gear]] of an engine.
# {{lb|en|baseball}} [[second base|Second base]].
# The agent of a party to an honour dispute whose role was to try to resolve the dispute or to make the necessary arrangements for a duel.<ref>https://www.theguardian.com/law/2016/oct/31/appeal-court-upholds-joint-enterprise-guilty-verdicts</ref>
# A [[Cub Scout]] appointed to assist the [[sixer]].
#: {{synonyms|en|seconder}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1995|author=Boy Scouts of Canada. National Council|title=The Cub Book
|passage=Many packs have a sixer's council where the sixers, and sometimes the '''seconds''', meet with Akela and some of the other leaders.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[second-class]] [[honours degree]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=William H. Cropper|title=Great Physicists|page=454
|passage=[Stephen Hawking] {{...}} would go to Cambridge, he said, if they gave him a first, and stay at Oxford if they gave him a '''second'''. He got a first.}}

