====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{rfm-sense|en}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[agree]] as a second person to (a proposal), usually to reach a necessary [[quorum]] of [[two]]. (See [[#Etymology 3|etymology 3]] for translations.)
#: {{ux|en|I '''second''' the motion.}}
# To follow in the next place; to [[succeed]].
#* {{RQ:Fuller Church History
|passage=In the method of nature, a low valley is immediately '''seconded''' with an ambitious hill.}}
#* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|passage=Sin is usually '''seconded''' with sin.}}
# {{lb|en|climbing}} To [[climb]] after a [[lead]] climber.

